I've audited both documents and written the two reports. Nothing suggests a certified value or a theorem claim is wrong. I ran only the offline `section2_figures --numbers` and read-only scripts over the caches, so nothing was fetched or overwritten. `tests/test_section2_figures.py` passes (3 tests).

**popularity.md** (58 claims): 44 reproduced, 3 match the record, 7 drift (all fixed), 1 stale (fixed), 3 unsourced. The unsourced ones are the 2026-09-17 network counts that were never cached: treewidth 6,222, bandwidth minimization 306, and the four raw unrestricted counts. One small claim, two real 1991 pathwidth works the rule misses, I matched to the record without re-searching the cache.

The three questions from the notes section:
- **(a) 1,213 vs 1,212:** the paper quotes 1,213, because that is what the figure draws, and footnotes 1,212 distinct. One record (`W4416062387`, 2026) came back twice. The footnote is now in the top table, the Figure 2.1 caption and the method paragraph (1,592 relevant and 2,270 hits, distinct). The duplicate is from 2026, so the heatmap's 1,014 is unaffected.
- **(b) Citation dates:** the citation column and the prose now use the 2026-09-29 cache, and the column is dated. I checked each value against the cache: Kinnersley 214, Kirousis & Papadimitriou 1986 293, Yanasse 1997 75, Ohtsuki 108. Works per Kinnersley citation goes from 5.6 to 5.7. A note says the unused scatter figure still draws the 09-17 counts; no point changes side of the diagonal.
- **(c) 74 vs 81:** both recomputed. It is 74 without Linhares & Yanasse (2002), split 72 spanning two disciplines and 2 spanning three, and 81 with it. "74 span two disciplines" is now "two or more".

Other fixes:
- "Almost all" multi-citing works stay in one discipline is now "most (195 of 269)".
- A dated note records two small breaks of the print spec: Figure 2.2's PDF is 6.51 in wide, and Figure 2.3's legend is 6.8 pt.

**plan.md** (48 claims): 17 reproduced, 26 match the record, 1 drift (fixed), 4 stale (dated notes added).
- **Drift:** "two `better_move` bugs found by the differential harness" is wrong. The first was found by profiling the C inner loop (`reports/better_move_bug.md`); only the second came from the harness.
- **Clarification:** "6,276 of 6,286 certificates" holds for the default configuration; it is 6,275 under `csearch`, with 0 rejected.
- **Stale:** the definite-move decision and remaining-work items 2, 3 and 5. Each now has a note: the fix has been the default since 2026-10-01, and 112 of 115 values are re-refuted with no answer changed. The `--summary` today shows 4 of the 7 at 125×125 refuted and 3 still running. The pathwidth reruns agree on all 11,424 graphs. Section 2 is done, and of the dataset work only the full run is left.
- Rome 11,183 / 11,534, 17,714 classes, 21,754 files, 16,087 certified, 10 of 11 VLSI circuits and the 37,800 / 6,747 ensembles all match their sources.

